==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Amber Egg: N106''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Mushroom Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
These forms are <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]], this unit is not meant to be used before its True Form. However, due to its somewhat low cost and quick recharge, it may be used as an emergency meatshield in [[Underground Labyrinth]] or [[Legend Quest]] if you have no use for its True Form.

==='''True Form'''===
Much like [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] against [[Casaurian Ahirujo]], Massive Damage in tandem with Behemoth Slayer results in truly insane DPS against Angel Behemoths like [[Angelic Beast Rajakong]], enough to counter the beast's also insanely high stats. Although Mushroom Cat has fairly short range, it's more than enough to outrange Rajakong's Omni Strike (only hits up to 250), and its wave immunity allows Mushroom Cat to stay safe from its occasional wave attacks, resulting in a very powerful counter. Outside of this enemy, Mushroom's great DPS and Area Attacks allow it to work well against many regular Angel pushers, many of which have low range. It finds even greater use when paired with the likes of [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo]] or [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen]], able to easily eradicate [[Gabriel]], [[Boraphim]], [[Angelic Gory]], [[Youcan]] and even [[St. Dober]]. Against other traits, the large amount of competition from higher ranged units, cheaper ones or more spammable ones results in him being rarely the best choice. It also works well as a general wave immune attacker, as its above-average stats allow it to counter wave enemies in stages where wave shields don't fare well. It may face a little bit of competition from other anti-Angel DPS options like [[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]], who has a lower cooldown, higher DPS, Curse Immunity and speed, and [[Phantom Cat (Rare Cat)|Bubble Cat]], who has higher range and LD coverage, but Mushroom has its own perks, most notably Wave Immunity and Behemoth Slayer. Treat the former two like [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] and [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] respectively and the latter like [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]].

He doesn't work well at all against foes that can hit behind their target with any means that isn't waves, nor against enemies that outrange him, like [[Angelic Sleipnir]].

